                      "author": {
                        "login": "omarbenhamid"
                      },
                      "body": "We need not to support Django QuerySet field lookups like `__startswith` and so. We just fail with a value error saying this is an unknown field: the MCP client shall use a $match stage to filter the query.\n",
                      "createdAt": "2026-09-12T16:15:37Z",
                      "updatedAt": "2026-09-12T16:40:04Z",
                      "url": "https://github.com/gts360/django-mcp-server/pull/72#discussion_r3996800581"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "PRRC_kwDOOns7hc71T0G4",
                      "databaseId": 4115612088,
                      "author": {
                        "login": "kemrec"
                      },
                      "body": "Fixed \u2014 an unresolved path segment now raises a ValueError instead of falling through, so a lookup/transform embedded in the bare key (e.g. `__startswith`) is rejected regardless of which field it's attached to, not just when it lands on an unpublished/excluded one.",
                      "createdAt": "2026-09-27T13:59:34Z",
                      "updatedAt": "2026-09-27T13:59:34Z",
                      "url": "https://github.com/gts360/django-mcp-server/pull/72#discussion_r4115612088"
                    }
                  ],
